republic-overreach.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P1 (S1): "more" is taken as take a larger share or advantage over another (pleonexia) in P1 P9 P10 and as outdo another in a craft's practice (exceed in saying or doing) where overlike is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r1.sense1)
republic-overreach.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another, fool, just, sage, sk1, unjust}; bad = {fool}, good = {sage}, ignorant = {fool}, like = {(another, another), (fool, fool), (just, just), (just, sage), (just, unjust), (sage, just), (sage, sage), (sage, unjust), (unjust, just), (unjust, sage), (unjust, unjust)}, overlike = {fool}, overlike_2 = {unjust}, overunlike = {fool, just, sage, unjust}, wise = {sage}
republic-overreach.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P1 (S1): "more" is taken as take a larger share or advantage over another (pleonexia) in P1 P9 P10 and as outdo another in a craft's practice (exceed in saying or doing) where overunlike is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r1.sense2)
republic-overreach.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another, fool, just, sage, sk1, unjust}; bad = {fool}, good = {sage}, ignorant = {fool}, like = {(another, another), (another, just), (fool, fool), (just, another), (just, just), (sage, sage), (unjust, unjust)}, overlike = {fool, unjust}, overunlike = {fool, sage}, overunlike_2 = {just, unjust}, wise = {sage}
republic-overreach.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: A2: it takes "more" from outdo in a craft's practice (the wise and the ignorant) to take a larger share or advantage (the just and the unjust), a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r1.sense3)
republic-overreach.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another, fool, just, sage, sk1, unjust}; bad = {fool}, good = {sage}, ignorant = {fool}, like = ∅, overlike = {fool, unjust}, overunlike = {fool, just, sage, unjust}, wise = {sage}
